# Stage 9e, Llama-3-8B-Instruct, direct code-word answer design: adversarial RL
# (2026-09-07). Reintroduces GRPO pressure on the SFT-seeded checkpoint
# (stage9e-llama-sft-code-word-v1/final_adapter), reusing Stage 9d's exact
# advantage-clamp + per-token-KL-clamp GRPOTrainer patch and checkpoint-isolation
# pattern unchanged. No decode-back-aware wrapper needed -- this design has no
# scaffolding line to carve out of the CoT penalty scan; plain score_completion_v2
# is used directly, with ground_truth being the CODE WORD (translated from the
# scenario's true final_answer_state before scoring, per code_word_answer_bank.py's
# own established pattern).

warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')
for _name in ('transformers', 'peft', 'accelerate', 'datasets', 'bitsandbytes', 'bitsandbytes.autograd._functions'):
    logging.getLogger(_name).setLevel(logging.ERROR)
